proof.text:
Write $B=A/I$, still a finite-type algebra over the algebraically closed field $k$. Every maximal ideal of $B$ is $\mathfrak m/I$ for a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $A$ containing $I$. By step 8 its localization is regular. The regular-closed-point smoothness statement supplies, for each such maximal ideal $\mathfrak q$, an element $g_{\mathfrak q}
otin\mathfrak q$ with $B_{g_{\mathfrak q}}$ smooth over $k$. The affine smoothness equivalence makes each $D(g_{\mathfrak q})$ a smooth open subscheme over $k$. These opens cover $\operatorname{Spec}B$: given a prime $\mathfrak p$, choose a maximal ideal $\mathfrak q\supseteq\mathfrak p$; then $g_{\mathfrak q}
otin\mathfrak q$ implies $g_{\mathfrak q}
otin\mathfrak p$. Smoothness local on the source proves that $\operatorname{Spec}B$ is smooth. If $B=0$ the empty family covers its empty spectrum and the same source-local statement applies.
